abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Closed formulas for both one-sided filtered F3 measures of Equation 10 of Ducuara, Susa and Skrzypczyk (arXiv:2406.03945), for every two-qubit state: the squared value is beta + eta + c^T Q (eta I - Q)^+ c in the steering-ellipsoid data of the other party, with eta from the largest real eigenvalue of an explicit 6x6 matrix. Every optimal filter, attainment by invertible filters, a rational criterion for values above one, an S6 obstruction to formulas in radicals and success-probability frontiers are included. Lean proves the main theorem for actual complex density matrices. The one-sided CHSH measures of Equation 9 are not treated. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
  - "quantum steering"
  - "local filtering"
  - "hidden quantum correlations"
